course: dictionary
lesson: 12660
title: Not the same: dissimilar
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dissimilar means not the same, different from each other. The start of the word, dis-, often means not, as in dislike and disagree. Similar means alike, so dissimilar means not alike. «The two puppies were dissimilar: one was black and fluffy, the other white and smooth.» The clues black and white, fluffy and smooth, show they are different.
explain: Watch out for «not dissimilar». The word not turns the meaning around. «The twins are not dissimilar» means they are quite alike. Ask: what is the sentence saying about how things are the same or different? Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
explain: You may also see dissimilar with the word to. «My handwriting is dissimilar to my sister's» means the two handwritings are different from each other. In maths, two shapes can be dissimilar if their sides and angles do not match in the same way.
fact: Dissimilar means not the same; different from each other.
fact: Dissimilar is an adjective, so it describes a noun: «dissimilar things», «dissimilar shapes».
fact: «Not dissimilar» means quite similar.
fact: The prefix dis- often means not or the opposite, as in dislike and disagree.
fact: Similar means alike, and dissimilar is its opposite.
exercise: «The two boats were dissimilar: one was a tiny rowing boat, the other a huge ferry.» What does dissimilar mean? | Very fast | Made of wood | Exactly the same | *Different from each other
exercise: «Their names are not dissimilar, as both start with the same letter.» What does not dissimilar mean? | *Quite alike | Hard to say | Very loud | Completely different
exercise: Which word means the opposite of similar? | *Dissimilar | Equal | Alike | Matching
test: «Her drawings are dissimilar to Ravi's.» What does dissimilar to show? | Things that are the same colour | *Things that are different from each other | Things that are very large | Things that are close friends
test: «Her drawings are not dissimilar to mine.» What does this mean? | *Her drawings are quite like mine | Her drawings are the best in the class | Her drawings are nothing like mine | Mine are better than hers
exam: «The two maps looked dissimilar, so Sam checked which one was correct.» What does dissimilar mean here? | Exactly the same | Sam's favourite | Folded up | *Not alike
